window.RB_INDEX = [{"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "What is RemBase?", "anchor": "what-is-rembase", "text": "RemBase is our new inventory system. It will replace Fishbowl on December 1, 2026 . RemBase has pages for stock, purchase orders, receiving, counting, production runs and Amazon shipments."}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "Until December 1: Fishbowl is real, RemBase is practice", "anchor": "until-december-1-fishbowl-is-real-rembase-is-practice", "text": "Do all real work in Fishbowl. Use RemBase only to practice. RemBase is copied from Fishbowl every night. The nightly copy does not touch TEST items, so your TEST practice stays. Practice on a real part is reset by the nightly copy. That is one more reason to practice only on TEST items. If you are not sure where to do something, do it in Fishbowl and ask Becca."}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "Practice only with TEST items", "anchor": "practice-only-with-test-items", "text": "Each person has their own practice PO and practice run: Person Receive this PO Build this run Count this bin Becca TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA TEST-PRACTICE-RUN-BECCA TEST-BIN Chad TEST-PRACTICE-CHAD TEST-PRACTICE-RUN-CHAD TEST-BIN Sabith TEST-PRACTICE-SABITH TEST-PRACTICE-RUN-SABITH TEST-BIN Practice in this order: 1. receive your PO, 2. count TEST-BIN, 3. build your run. Other TEST items: Type Name Parts TEST-COMP-A, TEST-COMP-B, TEST-KIT-2PK (a 2-pack made from A and B) Vendor TEST Vendor (practice) Used in the pictures PO TEST-HB-1, run TEST-HB-RUN-1 Practice making a PO by adding a line to your o"}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "How to open RemBase", "anchor": "how-to-open-rembase", "text": "Open the RemBase link that Becca sent you. Sign in with your work Airtable account. You see the menu on the left side. The RemBase menu on the left side of the screen"}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "The menu", "anchor": "the-menu", "text": "Page What it is for Inventory Find a part. See how much we have and where. Cycle Count Count the stock in a bin. Purchase Orders Make and track orders to vendors. Receiving See what is arriving from vendors. Run Planning Decide what to build next. Production Run Build kits and packs. Enter what you built. FBA Shipment Send stock to Amazon. Print box labels. Approvals Big stock changes that need a “yes” first. Flags Problems the system found. Returns Grading Check items that Amazon sent back to us. Backorders PO lines we are still waiting for. CC Orders Clear Conscience orders."}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "The most important rules", "anchor": "the-most-important-rules", "text": "Real work goes in Fishbowl until December 1. Practice only with TEST items. Some buttons send money, emails or orders. Read Do not press before you start. Not sure? Stop and ask Becca ."}, {"page": "index.html", "chapter": "Start here", "section": "About the pictures", "anchor": "about-the-pictures", "text": "Every picture comes from RemBase. A red box shows what to click or type. A red number is the step number. A red ✕ means do not press . An orange box means a real button : you may press it, but be careful. An orange $ means the button costs money . Black boxes hide private data such as prices, vendors, customers and Amazon numbers. You see the real data in RemBase."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "What this chapter is for", "anchor": "what-this-chapter-is-for", "text": "Every page in RemBase works the same way. Learn these few things once."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Pick a page", "anchor": "pick-a-page", "text": "Click a page name in the menu on the left. Some pages have smaller pages under them. Click the smaller page you need. The RemBase menu"}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Find something in a list", "anchor": "find-something-in-a-list", "text": "Most pages show a list. The buttons at the top right help you find things. Filter, Sort and Search buttons at the top right of a list Click the magnifying glass (Search). Type a part number, a name or a PO number. The list now shows only matching rows. To see everything again, click the ✕ in the search box. Filter hides rows you do not need. It changes only your own view. Sort changes the order of the rows. It changes only your own view."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Open a record", "anchor": "open-a-record", "text": "Click a row in the list. The record opens on the right side or in the middle."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Move between records and close", "anchor": "move-between-records-and-close", "text": "Arrows and close button at the top of an open record A – the arrows go to the previous or next record in the list. B – the ✕ closes the record."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "White boxes and grey text", "anchor": "white-boxes-and-grey-text", "text": "A white box with a border is a field you can type in. Grey text or text with no box is read-only. The system fills it in. RemBase saves what you type by itself. There is no Save button. Click outside the box or press Tab when you finish."}, {"page": "basics.html", "chapter": "Basics", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Typing in the wrong record. Check the title at the top before you type. Typing on a real part. Before December 1, type only on TEST items. Thinking a filter is gone. A number next to Filter or Sort means one is on. Click it to remove it."}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "Inventory shows every part. You can see how many we have in the warehouse and at Amazon, and in which bins. Who uses it: everyone looks here. Only Becca and Adam add new parts. For most people this page only shows information. You can look at real parts here. Do not change anything on a real part."}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "The list", "anchor": "the-list", "text": "Inventory list with stock columns A – Warehouse On Hand Qty: how many are in our warehouse. B – FBA On Hand Qty: how many are at Amazon. A dash (–) means no number yet."}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "Task: find a part and see its stock", "anchor": "task-find-a-part-and-see-its-stock", "text": "Click Inventory in the menu. Click the magnifying glass at the top right. Search button on the Inventory list Type the part number. For practice, type TEST-COMP-A . Search box with a part number typed in Click the part in the list. One search result: the practice part The part page opens. At the top you see the stock numbers. Top of the part page with stock numbers Scroll down. You see more sections: Lots, bin summary and ledger sections of a part 5 – Lots: each lot, its expiration date, its bin and how many are left. 6 – Part x Bin Summary: how many are in each bin. It updates every hour. 7 –"}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "For TEST-COMP-A after the practice receipt: Warehouse On Hand Qty = 24 One lot that expires 12/31/2027 in TEST-BIN One ledger line of type Receipt"}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "Task: add a new part (Becca and Adam only)", "anchor": "task-add-a-new-part-becca-and-adam-only", "text": "Only Becca and Adam add new parts. Everyone else: ask Becca to add the part. Click Inventory in the menu. Click New Part at the top right. New Part button at the top right of the Inventory page A form opens. Type the SKU (A). You must fill it in. Top of the New Part form with the SKU box marked Fill in the other boxes you know. Scroll down. Created via form (B) is ticked by itself. You cannot untick it. Click Create (C). Bottom of the New Part form with Created via form ticked and the Create button Always use New Part. A part made any other way (the data grid, an import, or Create “…” in a par"}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "Words on this page", "anchor": "words-on-this-page", "text": "Max Available to Build is not stock. For a pack, it is how many packs the parts can make. For a single part that goes into packs, it is what is left after the packs take their share. See Run Planning . Open PO Qty is how many are ordered but not received yet. FBA Inbound Qty is how many are on the way to Amazon."}, {"page": "inventory.html", "chapter": "Inventory", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Reading the wrong column. Warehouse and Amazon (FBA) are two different numbers. Expecting Part x Bin Summary right away. It can take up to one hour to update. Making a part another way. Only use New Part . A part made from a part list ( Create “…” ) is left out of planning. Pressing New Part if you are not Becca or Adam. Ask Becca to add the part."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "A purchase order (PO) is an order we send to a vendor. Each PO has lines . One line = one part and how many we ordered. Who uses it: Becca makes and sends POs. Everyone can look. Before December 1, make real POs in Fishbowl . In RemBase, practice only on your own practice PO (TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA, -CHAD or -SABITH). A brand-new PO you make before December 1 gets a PRACTICE- number, not a real PO number. Use the TEST Vendor and TEST parts on it. The pictures use TEST-HB-1."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Sub-pages", "anchor": "sub-pages", "text": "Sub-page What it is for Purchase Orders All POs. Open one to see its lines. PO Planning What we should order next. PO Planning – Commit Turns the planning ticks into POs. Becca only. PO Variance Report PO lines that came in short, over or damaged. Excluded from planning Parts that planning ignores, like TEST parts."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Task: find and open a PO", "anchor": "task-find-and-open-a-po", "text": "Click Purchase Orders in the menu. Find the PO in the list. For practice, use your own practice PO . Click the PO number. Purchase order list with the practice PO at the top The PO opens on the right. You see its status, vendor, dates, notes and lines. PO status: Issued – the PO is placed. Nothing has arrived yet. Partial – some of it has arrived. Fulfilled – everything has arrived. Closed Short – closed before everything arrived."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Task: add a line to a PO (practice)", "anchor": "task-add-a-line-to-a-po-practice", "text": "Open your own practice PO . Add a line for TEST-COMP-A or TEST-COMP-B . In PO Lines , click the + under the last line. Practice PO page with the add-line plus sign A new line appears. Click the + in its Part cell. Plus button inside the Part cell of a new line Type the part number. Click the right part in the list. Part picker showing the practice parts Never click Create “…” at the bottom of this list. It makes a new part that is left out of planning, and Becca gets a flag. If the part is missing, ask Becca to add it. Point at the new line. Click the expand button (two small arrows). Expand b"}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "PO status and Order Date", "anchor": "po-status-and-order-date", "text": "RemBase fills these in by itself: A new PO gets Status = Issued and today’s Order Date . When stock is received, the status changes to Partial or Fulfilled by itself. You only change the status by hand if Becca asks you to. Click the Status box and choose the status. Status list with Issued"}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "Finished practice PO with two lines Status Issued . When the stock arrives, it changes to Partial or Fulfilled by itself. (TEST-HB-1 is now Fulfilled , because both lines were received.) The lines are listed under PO Lines . Total Outstanding Qty = what has not arrived yet. Issued Warning: if a PO was already sent to the vendor, a change here does not reach the vendor. Tell the vendor yourself."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "To print a PO", "anchor": "to-print-a-po", "text": "Open the PO. Click the file under PO PDF . Print it from your browser. RemBase makes the PDF by itself and makes it again after every change. Do not upload or change it by hand. If the file is missing after a few minutes, ask Becca."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "PO Planning (look only)", "anchor": "po-planning-look-only", "text": "PO Planning shows what we should order. PO Planning list 1 – Recommended Order Qty: how many the system suggests we order. It covers the next 90 days of sales. It uses the last 30 days’ sales rate. It is adjusted for the season (more before the holidays). Clear Conscience lens and liquid show 0 . Consigned stock that we can buy any time covers them. PO Planning columns and the Commit button 2 – Planning Override Qty: Becca types her own number here. 3 – Start New PO: tick to start a new PO for this part. 4 – Planning Add To PO: tick to add this part to a PO. 5 – Commit / Clear: goes to the Com"}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "PO Planning – Commit (Becca only)", "anchor": "po-planning-commit-becca-only", "text": "Commit page with its two buttons marked do not press Commit PO Planning makes the POs from the ticked rows. Clear PO Planning Selections removes all the ticks. Do not press these unless you are Becca."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Excluded from planning", "anchor": "excluded-from-planning", "text": "Parts excluded from planning These parts are left out of planning. To bring a part back, Becca unticks Exclude from planning ."}, {"page": "purchase-orders.html", "chapter": "Purchase Orders", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Pressing Email PO. It emails the vendor. See Do not press . Clicking Create “…” in the part list. It makes a new part that planning leaves out. Ask Becca to add the part. Changing an Issued PO and not telling the vendor. RemBase does not tell them. Ticking boxes in PO Planning to “try it”. The ticks are shared with Becca’s real planning."}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "When boxes arrive from a vendor, you receive them. Receiving puts the stock in a bin with its expiration date. Who uses it: Chad and Sabith. Before December 1, receive real deliveries in Fishbowl . In RemBase, practice only on your own practice PO (TEST-PRACTICE-BECCA, -CHAD or -SABITH). The pictures use TEST-HB-1."}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "The Receiving page", "anchor": "the-receiving-page", "text": "Receiving list with the practice lines Click Receiving in the menu (1). Use Search (2) to find a PO number or a part. Each row is one PO line that still has something to receive. Click a row to see what was ordered and what has arrived. When everything on a line has arrived, the line leaves this list. During practice this list shows only TEST lines. Real parts are hidden on purpose. Until December 1, a receipt on a real part is blocked: the receipt line says Blocked – not posted , nothing is added to stock, and a Flag goes to Becca. Practice only on TEST POs."}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "Task: receive a PO line", "anchor": "task-receive-a-po-line", "text": "There are three ways to open the Receive form. All three open the same form. Way 1 is the easiest. Way 1 – from the Receiving page Click Receiving in the menu. Click your line (for practice: your own practice PO ). Scroll down to Received so far . Click Receive (3). Receive button on the Receiving page Way 2 – from Purchase Orders Click Purchase Orders in the menu. Click the PO number. In PO Lines , point at the line. Click the small expand icon (⤢) at the left of the row. A plain click on the row only selects a box, it does not open the line. The expand icon at the left of a PO line Next to R"}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "The receipt appears under Received so far (and under Receipt Lines on the PO line): Quantities and the receipt list after receiving Qty Received goes up. Outstanding Qty goes down. Derived Status says Partial or Fulfilled . Received so far lists each receipt with the bin, the expiration date, who received it, and Received At : the date and time in Eastern time. The stock is now on the part page in Inventory ."}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "Open POs", "anchor": "open-pos", "text": "Receiving → Open POs lists POs that are not finished, with how much is still outstanding. Click a PO to open it, then receive a line as in Way 2. Open POs list"}, {"page": "receiving.html", "chapter": "Receiving", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Typing cases in the Units box. Units = single items. Cases = full cases. No expiration date. Without a date the system cannot use the oldest stock first. Wrong bin. Choose the bin where the stock really is. Receiving twice. Look at Received so far before you receive. A wrong receipt. Do not try to fix it yourself. Ask Becca. ( Reverse this receipt is on the Do not press list.)"}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "A cycle count means you count what is really in one bin and compare it with RemBase. Who uses it: Chad and Sabith. Before December 1, do real counts in Fishbowl . In RemBase, practice only on TEST-BIN ."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Sub-pages", "anchor": "sub-pages", "text": "Sub-page What it is for Cycle Count All bins. Open a bin to count it. Count by Part All parts with their warehouse stock. Read-only."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Task: start a count", "anchor": "task-start-a-count", "text": "Click Cycle Count in the menu. Type the bin name in Search (1). For practice: TEST-BIN . Click the bin in the list. Scroll down to Count Sessions . Click Start Count Session (2). Bin page with the Start Count Session button A form opens. Counted By shows your name (A). Click Create (3). Start count form The new session appears under Count Sessions . Click it."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Task: enter your count", "anchor": "task-enter-your-count", "text": "RemBase makes one count line (4) for each part and lot in the bin. Expected is what RemBase thinks is there. Count session with its count lines Open the session. Click each line under Count Lines . Count that part in the bin. Type the number you counted in Actual Qty (6). Expected Qty (A) shows what RemBase thinks is there. A count line with Expected Qty and Actual Qty Close the line (✕ at the top right). Do the same for every line. When every line has a number, click Status and choose Completed (7). Status list with Completed Count every line. If you leave a line empty, RemBase skips it and c"}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "Finished count session The session status is Completed , with the time it was completed. The bin shows a new Last Counted Date . If your count was different, RemBase makes a Flag for Becca and changes the stock: a small difference (under the approval limit) changes the stock right away; a big difference waits in Approvals until Becca or Adam says yes."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Count by Part", "anchor": "count-by-part", "text": "Count by Part list This list shows each part and its warehouse stock. Use it to check a number. It is read-only."}, {"page": "cycle-count.html", "chapter": "Cycle Count", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Counting the wrong bin. Check the bin name at the top before you count. Leaving a line empty. RemBase skips it, so that part is not counted. Counting cases instead of units. Count single units. Starting two sessions for one bin. Look at Count Sessions first."}, {"page": "run-planning.html", "chapter": "Run Planning", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "Run Planning shows which products we should build and send to Amazon next. Who uses it: Becca and Adam decide. Chad can read it to see what is coming."}, {"page": "run-planning.html", "chapter": "Run Planning", "section": "The list", "anchor": "the-list", "text": "Run Planning list and its main columns 1 – Recommended Send Qty: how many the system suggests we build and send. It plans enough stock at Amazon for 45 days , plus the days Amazon needs to receive a shipment (about 12 days now; RemBase updates this every day). The list is sorted by this number. 2 – Run Planning Override Qty: Becca types her own number here to replace the suggestion. 3 – Run Planning Add To Run: tick to put this product in the next runs. 4 – Max Available to Build: how many we could build with the parts we have now. Days Of Cover FBA: how many days the stock at Amazon will last"}, {"page": "run-planning.html", "chapter": "Run Planning", "section": "Run Planning – Commit (Becca only)", "anchor": "run-planning-commit-becca-only", "text": "Run Planning commit page with buttons marked do not press Commit Run Planning makes production runs from the ticked rows. Clear Run Planning removes all the ticks. Planned runs lists the runs it made. Do not press these unless you are Becca."}, {"page": "run-planning.html", "chapter": "Run Planning", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Reading Max Available to Build as stock. It is not stock. Ticking Add To Run to “try it”. The ticks are shared. Becca’s next commit would use them. Thinking a number is wrong during the hourly update. Wait a few minutes."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "A production run is one job where we build a product from its parts. Example: a 2-pack is built from two single items. Who uses it: Chad and Sabith on the floor. Becca plans the runs. Before December 1, enter real runs in Fishbowl . In RemBase, practice only on your own practice run (TEST-PRACTICE-RUN-BECCA, -CHAD or -SABITH). Never press Finish Run on a real run before December 1. You may press it on your own practice run."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Sub-pages", "anchor": "sub-pages", "text": "Sub-page What it is for Production Run The office view: plan, components and lots. Production Run – Floor The floor view: what you built, cartons and pallet."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Task: find a run and check its parts", "anchor": "task-find-a-run-and-check-its-parts", "text": "Click Production Run in the menu. Click the run in the list (1). The list is sorted by due date. Production run page for the practice run Check Qty Planned (2). This is how many to build. Check Output Part . This is the product you build. Run Cartons (3) will show the boxes after you enter them on the Floor page. Scroll down to Run Components (4). Components the run will use, with lots Component Part SKU: each part you need. Qty To Consume: how many of that part. Chosen Lot (5): which lot to take. RemBase picks the lot that expires first. If Run Components is empty, RemBase has no recipe for t"}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Task: enter what you built (Floor page)", "anchor": "task-enter-what-you-built-floor-page", "text": "Click Production Run – Floor in the menu. Click your run in the list. Floor page with Qty Built and cartons Type the number you built in Qty Built (6). In Run Cartons , click the + (7) to add a carton row. Fill in the row. Press Tab to go to the next box: Boxes: how many boxes of this size. Units Per Box: how many units in each box. Length , Width , Height: box size in inches. Weight Per Box (lb): weight of one full box in pounds. If you have boxes of different sizes, add one row per size. If you built fewer than planned, choose a Short-Close Reason and write a Short-Close Note ."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "Floor page after typing the built quantity and cartons Qty Built shows your number. Run Stage changes to In Progress . Units in Run Cartons = Boxes × Units Per Box. It should match Qty Built. Missing is empty when the carton row is complete."}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Task: finish the run", "anchor": "task-finish-the-run", "text": "When the run is built and the cartons are entered, Finish Run takes the parts out of stock and adds the finished product. On a real run it also adds the units to the next Amazon shipment. Practice: you may press Finish Run on your own practice run . Your practice run is not linked to any Amazon shipment, and its Staging Pallet is TEST-BIN , so the finished TEST kits go to TEST-BIN. Do not change the Staging Pallet. Check Qty Built and the Run Cartons again. Click Finish Run at the top right. Press it once . Read Finish Result : DONE … – the run is finished. NOT DONE: … – nothing was changed. T"}, {"page": "production-run.html", "chapter": "Production Run", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Pressing Finish Run on a real run. Before December 1, only on your own practice run. Pressing Finish Run twice. Press once and read Finish Result . Units do not match Qty Built. Check Boxes × Units Per Box. Weight of the whole stack instead of one box. Type the weight of one box. Taking a different lot than Chosen Lot. Use the lot RemBase picked, or tell Becca."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "What this page is for", "anchor": "what-this-page-is-for", "text": "FBA means Amazon stores and ships our products. We send boxes to Amazon warehouses. This page plans those shipments, gets the labels and tracks what Amazon received. Who uses it: anyone on the team. Chad usually prints the labels and packs the boxes. The buttons on this page are REAL, not practice. They talk to Amazon for a real shipment. Confirm placement and Confirm freight cost money. Check the price first. Press a button once . Then wait until Inbound Pending is empty again. Not sure? Ask Becca before you press."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Sub-pages", "anchor": "sub-pages", "text": "Sub-page What it is for Sent to Amazon Every shipment we sent, and how much Amazon received. Next shipment The shipment we are building now. Labels are here. Sent from this plan The lines that went out with the last plan."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Task: check a shipment we sent", "anchor": "task-check-a-shipment-we-sent", "text": "Click FBA Shipment in the menu. Click Sent to Amazon (1). Click a shipment in the list (2). List of shipments sent to Amazon, ids hidden Read the numbers: One shipment with its numbers Status: Shipped, Receiving, Closed or Cancelled. Total Units: how many we sent. Qty Received By Amazon (3): how many Amazon has counted. Qty Remaining: how many Amazon has not counted yet. FBA Shipment Lines (4): one line per product."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "The Next shipment page", "anchor": "the-next-shipment-page", "text": "Next shipment page, ids, prices and labels hidden Read it from top to bottom: 1 – Inbound Pending: a button was pressed and RemBase is working on it. Wait. 2 – Inbound Result: the last message from RemBase. It tells you the next step. While Amazon is working it says what is happening, for example “Getting carrier quotes from Amazon. This takes a few minutes.” Wait until it changes. 3 – Label Files: the box labels, pallet labels and Bill of Lading (BOL). Ship Date , Freight Class: shipping details. Approved Placement Price , Approved Carrier Total: what Amazon and the carrier charge (hidden on "}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Task: print the box labels", "anchor": "task-print-the-box-labels", "text": "Open FBA Shipment → Next shipment . Read Inbound Result . It says when the labels are ready. Under Label Files , click the file you need. The files come in two steps: After Confirm placement : the two box label files. After Confirm freight (truck / LTL shipments only): the pallet labels and the bill of lading . The files: box labels letter 6-up – six labels on one letter page. box labels 4x6 thermal – for the label printer. pallet labels – Amazon gives four labels for each pallet , one for each side. bill of lading – the paper for the truck driver. The file opens. Print it. Put one box label o"}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Sent from this plan", "anchor": "sent-from-this-plan", "text": "FBA Shipment → Sent from this plan lists each product line that went out with the last plan: how many units, when, and which Amazon shipment it went in. It is read-only. Lines sent from the last plan, ids hidden"}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "The buttons, in order (real buttons: be careful)", "anchor": "the-buttons-in-order-real-buttons-be-careful", "text": "Anyone on the team may press these for a real shipment. They work on any open shipment that is not a TEST shipment. Read what each one does first. Button What it does Create plan Starts a new shipment plan with Amazon. Refresh options Asks Amazon again for warehouse choices. Confirm placement Accepts the Amazon warehouse choice. Costs money. Get prices again Asks carriers for new prices. Does not cost money. Confirm freight Books the carrier. Costs money. Re-check Asks Amazon for the latest status. Cancel plan Cancels the plan with Amazon. Mark as sent Tells RemBase the boxes left our building"}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "What you should see", "anchor": "what-you-should-see", "text": "After a button press, Inbound Pending shows a message, then clears. Inbound Result then says what happened and what to do next. After Confirm placement , the two box label files appear under Label Files . After Confirm freight (truck shipments), the pallet labels and the bill of lading appear too."}, {"page": "fba-shipment.html", "chapter": "FBA Shipment", "section": "Common mistakes", "anchor": "common-mistakes", "text": "Pressing a button twice because nothing seems to happen. Wait for Inbound Pending to clear. Using old labels. Always print from the shipment you are packing. Wrong label size. Use 4x6 for the thermal printer and 6-up for normal paper. Confirming without checking the price. Confirm placement and Confirm freight cost money. Practicing on this page. These buttons are real. There is no TEST shipment."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "Approvals", "anchor": "approvals", "text": "What it is for: some stock changes are big, for example a large count difference or a disposal. They wait here for a “yes” before they change the stock. Who uses it: Becca and Adam. What you see: Approvals → Ledger lists the waiting changes. Most days it is empty. Do not approve anything unless you are Becca or Adam."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "Flags", "anchor": "flags", "text": "What it is for: a flag is a problem the system found. Examples: a part with no vendor, a count difference, a short Amazon shipment. Who uses it: Becca. Others may be assigned a flag. Sub-page What it shows My Open Flags Flags assigned to you. All Open Flags Every open flag. Open flags list To work on a flag: Click the flag. Read the Title and Note . Fix the cause in the right place, or ask Becca. When it is fixed, set Status to Resolved ."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "Returns Grading", "anchor": "returns-grading", "text": "What it is for: Amazon sends products back to us (removal orders). We check each item and decide what to do with it. Who uses it: Sabith. Returns grading page, order ids hidden The list shows each returned product and how many we expect. After December 1, for each item: Count the items. Type the number in Received Qty (1). Choose a grade (2). Choose a Disposition (3): what we do with it. If you keep it, choose the Putaway Bin (4) and the Expiration Date . Before December 1, look only. Do not type on this page unless Becca asks."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "Backorders", "anchor": "backorders", "text": "What it is for: PO lines that are still waiting for stock from the vendor. Who uses it: Becca. Everyone can look. Backordered PO lines, costs hidden This page is read-only. Click a line to see its PO."}, {"page": "other-pages.html", "chapter": "Other pages", "section": "CC Orders", "anchor": "cc-orders", "text": "What it is for: orders that Clear Conscience sends us for their customers. We pack and ship them. Who uses it: Sabith and Becca. CC Orders list, customer data hidden Before December 1, look only. Real CC orders are still handled the old way."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Do not press", "anchor": "", "text": "Do not press any button on this page. These buttons email vendors, move real stock or delete records. If you think one is needed, ask Adam or Becca first ."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Email PO", "anchor": "email-po", "text": "Email PO button marked do not press It emails the PO to the vendor."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Delete PO", "anchor": "delete-po", "text": "Delete PO in the menu, marked do not press It is inside the … menu on a PO. It deletes the PO."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Email Staged POs and Delete Staged POs", "anchor": "email-staged-pos-and-delete-staged-pos", "text": "Email and delete staged POs buttons marked do not press They are at the bottom of the Purchase Orders list. They email or delete every staged PO at once."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Reverse this receipt", "anchor": "reverse-this-receipt", "text": "Reverse this receipt button marked do not press It undoes a receipt. If a receipt is wrong, ask Becca."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Production buttons", "anchor": "production-buttons", "text": "Finish Run on a real run – moves stock and adds units to the next Amazon shipment. (On your own practice run it is OK.) Reverse Run – undoes a finished run. See Production Run ."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Planning buttons (Becca only)", "anchor": "planning-buttons-becca-only", "text": "Commit PO Planning and Clear PO Planning Selections Commit Run Planning and Clear Run Planning"}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Anything else", "anchor": "anything-else", "text": "Delete on any record. Create “…” in a part list. It makes a new part that planning leaves out. Ask Becca to add the part. New Part – Becca or Adam only. See Inventory . Add found item in a count. When in doubt: stop and ask ."}, {"page": "do-not-press.html", "chapter": "Do not press", "section": "Real buttons: be careful (Amazon shipments)", "anchor": "real-buttons-be-careful-amazon-shipments", "text": "The Amazon buttons on FBA Shipment → Next shipment are not on the do-not-press list. Anyone on the team may press them for a real shipment. They are real, not practice: The shipment buttons in the … menu Create plan , Refresh options , Re-check , Get prices again , Cancel plan , Mark as sent Confirm placement and Confirm freight cost money. Check the price first. Press once , then wait until Inbound Pending is empty. See FBA Shipment for what each button does."}, {"page": "glossary.html", "chapter": "Glossary", "section": "Glossary", "anchor": "", "text": "Word Meaning Bin A place on a shelf where stock is kept. Each bin has a name, like 01-A3. Lot One group of the same part with the same expiration date in the same bin. Expiration date The “use by” date on the box. FEFO “First expired, first out”. Use the stock that expires first. RemBase picks lots this way. Ledger The list of every stock move: receipts, runs, counts, shipments. On hand How many we have now. PO (purchase order) An order we send to a vendor. PO line One part on a PO, with its quantity and price. Vendor The company we buy from. Receipt The record that stock arrived. Outstanding "}, {"page": "who-to-ask.html", "chapter": "Who to ask", "section": "Who to ask", "anchor": "", "text": "Question Ask Anything about RemBase or practice Becca Purchase orders, planning, flags Becca Warehouse work, bins, counting, building Chad Any button on the Do not press list Adam or Becca , before you press Amazon shipments Anyone may press the shipment buttons. Not sure? Ask Becca first."}, {"page": "who-to-ask.html", "chapter": "Who to ask", "section": "When you ask, send", "anchor": "when-you-ask-send", "text": "The page name (for example: Receiving). The record name (for example: TEST-HB-1). What you clicked. What you expected to see. What you saw instead. A screenshot helps."}, {"page": "who-to-ask.html", "chapter": "Who to ask", "section": "Remember", "anchor": "remember", "text": "Until December 1, real work goes in Fishbowl . Practice only with TEST items. Not sure? Stop and ask. It is always OK to ask."}];
